    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Dean--Williams-College-of-Business--WCB--Undergraduate-Programs_JR100825": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean, Williams College of Business (WCB) Undergraduate Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Dean, Williams College of Business (WCB) Undergraduate Programs ‌ Xavier University is seeking a dedicated and mission-driven Assistant Dean for the Undergraduate Program in the Williams College of Business to provide strategic leadership and operational oversight for undergraduate student success. This role leads and supports initiatives related to academic administration, advising, enrollment management, retention, persistence, and timely degree completion while serving as a key resource for students, faculty, and families. The Assistant Dean collaborates closely with faculty, staff, and campus partners to promote academic excellence and a student-centered experience. The successful candidate will be a thoughtful problem solver, strategic partner, and strong communicator who can navigate complex academic policies, support student advocacy, and advance initiatives that strengthen undergraduate programs and services. Grounded in Xavier’s Jesuit mission and commitment to cura personalis , this position plays an essential role in educating the whole person and fostering an inclusive environment where business students can learn, grow, and thrive. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: Academic Policies & Processes: Implement academic policies, manage student academic processes, and ensure compliance with university and accreditation standards. Undergraduate Programs & Operations: Support undergraduate programs, experiential learning, student organizations, scholarships, and co-curricular initiatives. Advising & Retention: Provide student-centered advising and support initiatives that promote retention, persistence, and timely graduation. Student Support & Advocacy: Advocate for students and connect them with campus resources to address academic, personal, and financial challenges. Recruitment, Enrollment & Course Management: Support recruitment, enrollment, registration, course scheduling, and data-informed enrollment planning. JOB REQUIREMENTS: Master’s degree in Education, Business Administration (MBA), or a related field. To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University's website.  Applications will be reviewed immediately and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.  Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor-of-Instruction--Division-of-Physiology-and-Pathology_JR100800": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction, Division of Physiology and Pathology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor of Instruction, Division of Physiology and Pathology ‌ The proposed College of Osteopathic Medicine at Xavier University (XUCOM) invites applications for non-tenure-track physiology or pathology faculty in the Division of Physiology and Pathology. The 12-month position beginning in June of 2027 are involved in the creation, development, and delivery of the basic science medical curriculum, the creation and evaluation of assessments and provide mentorship and guidance for medical students. The biomedical science faculty report to the Associate Dean of Faculty and Medical Programs. XUCOM is the first osteopathic medical school at a Jesuit Catholic University. To fulfill its mission, XUCOM will integrate Jesuit Catholic traditions and values with Osteopathic Principles and Practice; our mission is infused in all that we do. Xavier is an EOE. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES:   Designs and delivers curricular content within the College of Osteopathic Medicine Involved in the creation of assessments within the curriculum of the College of Osteopathic Medicine Advises and mentors students of XUCOM Contributes to the mission of the college through teaching and service Other duties as assigned QUALIFICATIONS:           Required: Terminal degree in discipline related to medical education (PhD, MD, DO)           Preferred: 1-3 years teaching experience in medical education or graduate education Evidence of student mentoring Applicants with expertise in histopathology and/or pathophysiology will be especially considered POSITION: Twelve-month, non-tenure track positions RANK/SALARY: Rank and salary commensurate with qualifications and experience HOW TO APPLY: To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter, resume, teaching philosophy and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University's website. Position will remain open until filled. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
