    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Adjunct-Clinical-Teaching-Assistant--Pre-Licensure-Programs--College-of-Nursing_JR100492": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Teaching Assistant, Pre-Licensure Programs, College of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Clinical Teaching Assistant, Pre-Licensure Programs, College of Nursing ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates to join our pool of potential adjunct faculty for the 2026-2027 academic year. This posting is intended to collect applications for in-person, part-time, non-tenure-track position for an Adjunct Instructor within the Xavier University College of Nursing. Candidates must be dedicated to graduate or undergraduate teaching and demonstrate excellence in their field.  The successful candidate will contribute to our commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Applications will be accepted on a continuous basis, and candidates may be contacted as teaching needs arise. Adjunct faculty contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis, depending on departmental needs and student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications (as evidenced on the resume): Active RN Ohio Licensure with number(s) clearly listed. Two years of employment in the course subject area. Preferred: 2 years of employment within the past 5 years (ex: med-surg, mental health, pediatrics, critical care, etc.) BSN Degree, MSN preferred (only applicable to positions in the BSN prelicensure program) must demonstrate current certifications, preceptor/orienting experience, annual continuing education, list of graduate courses completed and expected graduation date(s). MSN Degree (required for positions in the MIDAS prelicensure program).  A separate self-disclosed competency of basic nursing skills and procedures may be required.   Duties include: Assist and work at the direction of a faculty member (course coordinator) providing instruction in the laboratory and/or clinical setting. Attend and follow the assigned clinical agency orientation and guidelines. Must be medically cleared and able to perform to Xavier and hospital(s) policies. Facilitate the student’s clinical experience to achieve the objectives of the nursing course. Clarify with the faculty member (course coordinator/lead); the role of the teaching assistant in each course the responsibilities of the faculty member regarding final grades the course and clinical objectives the clinical experience evaluation tool(s)   Demonstrate the ability to model professional behavior, communicate effectively, and utilize best practice (evidenced based) guidelines in the clinical and/or laboratory setting that reflects current nursing practice/standards. Follow Xavier University College of Nursing and the clinical facilities’ policies on protected health information. Model the mission, vision, and values of Xavier University College of Nursing. Contribute to the evaluation of the student’s performance by providing timely and constructive feedback to the faculty member (course coordinator/lead) and the student regarding the student's achievement of established objectives, including grading of assignments and completion of evaluation forms.  Assist and instruct the student in collaborating with nursing and other healthcare professionals during the following: Developing critical thinking and clinical judgment skills to provide safe and effective nursing care. Collecting pertinent data Analyzing the data Identifying expected patient outcomes Developing a plan that describes strategies and alternatives to obtain expected outcomes. Implementing the identified plan, including coordination of care delivery. For additional information, please contact Amy Wilson, Nursing Clinical and Lab Manager, The College of Nursing, battagliaa@xavier.edu . To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University’s website.  Please note: This adjunct faculty pool will close on May 30, 2027 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new adjunct pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Adjunct-Faculty--School-of-Education_JR100264": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, School of Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Faculty, School of Education ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates to join our pool of potential adjunct faculty to serve as supervisors of teacher candidates for the 2026-2027 academic year. This posting is intended to collect applications for part-time, non-tenure-track position for an Adjunct Instructor in the School of Education . Candidates must be dedicated to graduate or undergraduate teaching and demonstrate excellence in their field.   The successful candidate will contribute to our commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Applications will be accepted on a continuous basis , and candidates may be contacted as teaching needs arise. Adjunct faculty contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis , depending on departmental needs and student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications: ·        Master’s degree in Education or a related field, minimum 5 years K-12 teaching experience, and extensive related experience (e.g., published, leadership, etc.) in the education field or terminal degree in a related field and 5 years K12 teaching experience. ·        Currently hold and maintain a valid professional educator license. ·        Flexible availability during the school day is necessary. ·        University supervisors will need to be proficient with technology such as email, inputting observation notes, fillable PDFs, and other basic computer skills. ·        University supervisors will serve as a liaison between Xavier University and the field placement, so effective and direct communication skills are necessary. Duties include: ·        University supervisors will be required to travel to school sites each semester as designated by the Field Coordinator. ·        Supervisors are expected to observe teacher candidates throughout the semester and provide feedback regarding teacher candidate performance in the areas of dispositions and pedagogy. ·        Successful supervisors will be able to connect with undergraduate and graduate students to create positive mentorships. ·        Supervisors will guide, engage and support teacher candidates throughout their development as novice teachers. ·        Clear and consistent communication with both the teacher candidate and cooperating teacher is required. ·        Being the first point of contact for both teacher candidate and cooperating, and troubleshooting issues that might arise ·        Student Teaching Supervision – requires 4-6 site visits ·        Methods/Clinicals Supervision – requires 1-2 site visits For additional information, please contact Dr. Jody Googins, Co-Director of the School of Education, googinsj@xavier.edu , 513-745-2821.   To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University’s website.   Please note: This adjunct faculty pool will close on May 31, 2027 If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new adjunct pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Teaching-Professor--Division-Chair-of-Family-Medicine_JR100207": {
      "title": "Teaching Professor, Division Chair of Family Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Teaching Professor, Division Chair of Family Medicine ‌ Xavier University invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure-track Chair of the Division of Family Medicine in its proposed College of Osteopathic Medicine (XUCOM), beginning Summer 2026. This senior academic leadership role provides the opportunity to shape the Family Medicine division within a mission-driven osteopathic medical school at a Jesuit Catholic university. The Chair will lead curricular integration across preclinical and clinical phases, serve as Clinical Clerkship Director for third-year Family Medicine rotations, mentor faculty and students, and ensure divisional excellence in accreditation, assessment, and strategic planning. This is a 0.8 FTE academic appointment. The successful candidate is expected to maintain clinical privileges and provide patient care approximately one day per week within a partner health system. Qualifications: DO or MD degree. Current AOA or ABMS board certification in Family Medicine. Eligibility for unrestricted Ohio medical licensure. Eligibility for clinical privileges at a partner health system. Minimum of 5 years of progressive leadership experience in undergraduate or graduate medical education. Minimum of 10 years of clinical practice experience in Family Medicine. Experience mentoring faculty. Experience with accreditation processes. Experience developing assessment items for NBOME or NBME. Budget management experience in an academic or healthcare setting. Job Responsibilities: Lead the development, delivery, and continuous improvement of Family Medicine curricular content across preclinical and clinical years. Serve as Clinical Clerkship Director for third-year Family Medicine rotations. Mentor and evaluate division faculty and medical students, including career advising and residency preparation. Ensure divisional compliance with COCA accreditation standards and support institutional strategic initiatives. Oversee divisional operations, including faculty workload distribution, committee assignments, and budget administration. Additional responsibilities include contributing to teaching, scholarship, service, and student engagement activities in support of the College’s mission. Applications Process To ensure consideration, qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae and three professional references through Xavier University’s website. Review of applications will begin March 23, 2026 , and will continue until the position closes at the University’s discretion. About Xavier University Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Adjunct-Faculty---PPP-Sophomore-Year-Politics-and-Power-Block_JR100119-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - PPP Sophomore Year Politics and Power Block",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Faculty - PPP Sophomore Year Politics and Power Block ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates to join our pool of potential adjunct faculty for the 2026-2027 academic year. This posting is intended to collect applications for part-time, non-tenure-track position for an Adjunct Instructor in Philosophy, Politics and the Public. Candidates must be dedicated to undergraduate teaching and demonstrate excellence in their field.   The successful candidate will contribute to our commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Applications will be accepted on a continuous basis, and candidates may be contacted as teaching needs arise. Adjunct faculty contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis, depending on departmental needs and student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications: ·        5 years’ experience in the field of politics and civic engagement, including but not limited to: legislative work; policy advocacy or fundraising; campaign work; nonprofit policy work, etc.   ·        A qualified candidate might hold in addition to the above a M.A. or Ph.D. in a field related to the above work. Duties include: ·        Teaching PPUB 210: Campaign, Politics and Media in the fall and PPUB 211: Public Policy Practice in the spring. Both courses are 3 credits and meet TR for 75-85 minutes each. For additional information, please contact Dr. Kathleen Smythe, Professor, History, smythe@xavier.edu . To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University’s website.   Please note: This adjunct faculty pool will close on January 30, 2027 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new adjunct pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Columbus-OH/Adjunct-Faculty-ABSN-Track--Columbus--OH---College-of-Nursing_JR100068": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty ABSN Track, Columbus, OH - College of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Faculty ABSN Track, Columbus, OH - College of Nursing ‌ Xavier University is seeking qualified candidates to join our pool of potential adjunct faculty for the 2026-2027 academic year. This posting is intended to collect applications for part-time, non-tenure-track position for an Adjunct Instructor in the Accelerated Bachelor of Nursing in Science (ABSN) track. Candidates must be dedicated to graduate or undergraduate teaching and demonstrate excellence in their field.  The successful candidate will contribute to our commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Applications will be accepted on a continuous basis , and candidates may be contacted as teaching needs arise. Adjunct faculty contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis , depending on departmental needs and student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications: Completed an approved registered nursing education program Have at least two years of experience in the practice of nursing as a registered nurse Baccalaureate degree in nursing; graduate degree preferred Current, unencumbered licensure as a registered nurse in Ohio and in state of practicum setting, if applicable.   Duties include: Planning the student’s clinical experience at the direction of the faculty member support appropriate to the clinical situation contribute to the evaluation the student’s performance supervise, teach, and evaluate up to 8 students in the clinical settings as well as guide students through simulation experiences based on course objectives and student learning needs For additional information, please contact: Jessica Barsa, MSN, RN, BCEN Clinical Operations Coordinator Xavier University College of Nursing, ABSN Jessica.barsa@absn.xavier.edu To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University’s website.  Please note: This adjunct faculty pool will close on May 31, 2026 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new adjunct pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Executive-Assistant--Office-of-the-Provost_JR100843": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant, Office of the Provost",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Executive Assistant, Office of the Provost ‌ Xavier University is seeking a highly organized, proactive, and service-oriented  Executive Assistant  to provide confidential administrative support to the Provost and Chief Academic Officer (CAO) and the Office of the Provost. This position plays a key role in supporting the day-to-day operations of the Provost and CAO's office, coordinating complex calendars and meetings, facilitating communication with University leaders and external stakeholders, and ensuring that important administrative priorities are handled efficiently and effectively. The Executive Administrative Assistant will work closely with the Provost and CAO, Associate Provosts, Associate Vice President, University administrators, Board of Trustees members and their assistants, faculty, staff, and external partners. The successful candidate will demonstrate exceptional judgment, professionalism, discretion, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced university environment. Job Responsibilities: Support the Provost and Chief Academic Officer Manage and coordinate the extensive calendar and meeting schedule for the Provost and CAO, ensuring recurring meetings and critical commitments are scheduled and completed in a timely manner. Anticipate meeting needs and coordinate with University offices to gather materials and complete advance work. Track and follow up on action items resulting from meetings. Provide administrative support for the Board of Trustees' Academic Affairs Committee and related working groups. Assist with the University's rank and tenure process and provide support to the University Rank & Tenure Committee. Prepare memos, correspondence, and other materials for review and signature by the Provost and CAO. Maintain and update distribution lists, email lists, committee records, and related documents. Communicate and distribute information on behalf of the Provost and CAO. Coordinate travel arrangements for the Provost and CAO. Maintain the Academic and University Committees document. Support the annual Academic Program Check-in process. Perform other administrative duties in support of the Provost and CAO as assigned. Support the Office of the Provost Serve as the welcoming first point of contact for visitors to the Office of the Provost. Coordinate meeting schedules and calendars for the Associate Provost for Strategic Initiatives, Associate Provost for Academic Engagement, Associate Provost for Academic Excellence, and Associate Vice President for Provost Budget and Planning. Proactively identify opportunities to improve the quality, efficiency, responsiveness, and effectiveness of administrative services provided by the Provost and CAO team. Schedule and coordinate use of conference rooms & coordinate monthly team meetings. Arrange meeting room setups, catering, supplies, technology, and other logistical needs. Serve as a Buyer in Workday for the Office of the Provost. Reconcile Provost Area purchasing cards in Workday. Maintain office supplies and place orders as needed. Serve as a backup Building Coordinator for Schmidt Hall. Prepare and distribute communications and memos on behalf of members of the Office of the Provost and others conducting business within the Provost Area. Update Provost Area webpages as needed. Perform other duties in support of the Office of the Provost as assigned. Activity and Event Collaboration Coordinate the University’s spring Academic Honors Celebration. Support faculty recognition activities associated with the University’s employee recognition ceremony. Collaborate on special projects and University initiatives as assigned. Qualifications: Associate’s degree required. Three to five years of related administrative experience. At least one year of experience providing administrative support to an executive senior leader, or comparable position. To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University’s website.  Applications will be reviewed immediately and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion. Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Building-Aid---Substitute-Teacher--St-Peter-Faber-Academy_JR100839": {
      "title": "Building Aid & Substitute Teacher, St. Peter Faber Academy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Building Aid & Substitute Teacher, St. Peter Faber Academy ‌ St. Peter Faber Academy is seeking a Building Aid & Substitute Teacher who will support the daily operations of the school by assisting teachers, supervising students, and providing classroom coverage when needed. This position helps maintain a safe, positive, and productive learning environment while supporting the academic, social, and emotional growth of students. The Building Aid/Substitute Teacher will assist classroom teachers with instructional activities and classroom management, supervise students during arrival, dismissal, lunch, recess, transitions, provide support for students individually or in small groups under teacher direction, assist with preparation of classroom materials, help maintain a clean, organized, and safe school environment, support office staff and school-wide events as needed, monitor student behavior and reinforce school expectations and policies, and maintain confidentiality regarding students, staff, and school matters. Interested candidates must have High School Diploma or equivalent.  Associate or Bachelor’s Degree is preferred. At least 3 years in a similar role with comparable goals and responsibilities. Ability to adapt to a changing environment and handle multiple priorities. Excellent writing and analytical skills. Proficient in Microsoft Office, with aptitude to learn new software and systems. Applications will be reviewed immediately and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.  Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. St. Peter Faber Academy is a Preschool-5th grade laboratory school that is connected to Xavier University.  Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Home-Remote/Adjunct-Faculty---MS-in-Water-Utilities-Management_JR100847": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - MS in Water Utilities Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Faculty - MS in Water Utilities Management ‌ Xavier University is seeking a qualified candidate to join our team of adjunct faculty in the Master of Science in Water Utilities Management program for the 2027-2028 academic year. Program Website: https://www.xavier.edu/water-utilities-management/index We are seeking applications for a part-time, non-tenure-track, remote Adjunct faculty position teaching online in the Water Utilities Management graduate program . All courses are fully online and asynchronous. The current opening is below: WMGT 620 Capital Planning and Asset Management (2 CH) This course serves as a culminating experience that integrates utility finance, rate setting, and operational fundamentals into long-term capital planning and asset management decisions. Students learn to evaluate infrastructure condition, risk, and lifecycle costs to prioritize investments and develop defensible capital improvement plans (CIPs). Emphasis is placed on aligning capital planning with financial capacity, rate impacts, regulatory requirements, and service level goals. Through applied cases and scenario analysis, students synthesize technical, financial, and policy considerations to support sustainable, long-term utility decision-making. Prerequisites: WMGT 570 Finance Fundamentals, WMGT 610 Rate Setting and Utility Finance Course Build: Begins January 2027, Course Launch: August 2027 Candidates must be dedicated to graduate teaching and demonstrate excellence in their relevant field. The successful candidate will contribute to our commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Applications will be accepted on a continuous basis until the position is filled. Adjunct faculty contracts are issued on a semester-by-semester basis , depending on program needs and student enrollment. Minimum Qualifications: Required: A master's degree or beyond in the discipline in which the instructor is teaching and exceptional tested experience that has been validated through publication or public recognition. Examples of tested experience may include 5 years of experience in the given subject matter plus at least one of the following: professional publications in a field related to the subject matter recognition of achievement in a field related to the subject matter professional credentials earned in a field related to the subject matter other significant contributions in a field related to the subject matter (i.e., evidence of “tested experience”) relevant to the graduate coursework being taught. Duties include: Complete Xavier’s 6-week Introduction to Online Course Design course (begins January, 2027). Lead a 7-week MS in Water Utilities Management online course which includes Timely response to student emails, hosting virtual calls with students Communicating with students throughout coursework Interacting with students in discussion boards and on assignments Grading assignments in a timely manner Compensation: $1,000 per course credit hour for training and course development $2,000 per course credit hour for course instruction For additional information, please contact Dr. Justin Roush, Program Director and Associate Professor of Economics, Economics Department, roushj2@xavier.edu. To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resume, Teaching Statement, and the names and contact information of three professional references. The Teaching Statement should focus on the candidate’s vision for teaching this course at Xavier University. Email materials to roushj2@xavier.edu . Please specify in your cover letter and the subject line of the email the position for which you are applying.   Please note: This application window will close on December 15th, 2026 . If you are not contacted by this time and remain interested in employment with Xavier University, please reapply to a new adjunct pool posting once it becomes available. Xavier University is an equal opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Pre-Health-Professions-Advisor_JR100844": {
      "title": "Pre-Health Professions Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Pre-Health Professions Advisor ‌ Xavier University’s College of Arts and Sciences is seeking applications for the position of Pre-Health Professions Advisor.  The advisor will assume a leadership role in the determination of support services to pre-professional health students at Xavier.  Along with the Chair of the Health Sciences Committee, the Advisor also facilitates all aspects of a student’s progress in preparing for a career in one of the health professions.  The Advisor serves as the primary contact person with professional health schools and initiates and administers programs and events with these schools. JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: Advise students in all aspects of their applications and preparation for admissions tests to professional health schools, including developing information sessions, leading workshops, providing resources, and increasing advising consultation during the application cycle. Develop and direct activities and programs for Xavier pre-professional health students that focus on developing better understanding of health and career-related issues.  Provide regular in-person and remote events to ensure information is accessible to students at every stage. Direct and manage the multiple responsibilities of the Health Professions Committee in coordination with the Chair, while also participating as a member of this Committee. Administer Xavier’s Pre-Professional Health Advisory Program (PPHAP), and serve as liaison for the undergraduate pathway to Xavier’s College of Osteopathic Medicine.  Serve as the primary Staff/Faculty Advisor for the Pre-Medical Society, Pre-Dental Society, and Alpha Epsilon Delta, and provide administrative staff support for their programming. Administer and manage all record-keeping and tracking of student applications, recommendations and academic records in support of the professional school application process. JOB REQUIREMENTS: Master’s degree required in Counseling, Communications, or Science areas A Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of 3 years of work experience in student affairs or academic career advising in higher education or healthcare may substitute for a Master’s degree. Strong interpersonal skills in dealing sensitively with a wide variety of constituents, including students, parents, faculty, and professional school representatives Ability to work independently, creatively and collaboratively in an organized manner Ability to handle multiple tasks and meet established deadlines in a fast-paced environment The position is part of Xavier Health, the University's integrated health initiative connecting a broad portfolio of programs and creating opportunities for collaboration across disciplines.  Xavier Health offers more than 15 undergraduate and 12 graduate pathways, more than 500 community partnership sites, and connections across disciplines that contribute to health and human well-being. Xavier Health prepares servant-leaders through real-world experiences and Jesuit Catholic formation that puts the whole person at the center of care.  Xavier University in Cincinnati, Ohio is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal art and is strongly committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity.  These values are central to our mission.  We strive for a climate of respect and inclusiveness that welcomes and supports members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences, is committed unreservedly to open and free inquiry, and deliberately seeks out multiple perspectives. To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter, resume and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University's website.  The review of applications will start on October 1, 2026 .  Applications will continue to be accepted until the position closes at the university’s discretion. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor--Criminal-Justice_JR100862-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor, Criminal Justice ‌ The Department of Criminal Justice at Xavier University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning in August 2027. We seek a collaborative teacher-scholar whose teaching and research will strengthen the Department’s expertise in criminal justice research methods, policing broadly defined, or both. The teaching expectation is 18 credit hours annually for this tenure-track faculty position when a faculty member meets the College’s active scholarship standards.   The Department has a robust undergraduate and growing online graduate program. We offer bachelor’s and master’s degrees in criminal justice, a dual degree (MSN/MS CJUS) with nursing, and a post-baccalaureate criminal justice administration certificate for working professionals. Consistent with Xavier University’s mission, the Department seeks to equip undergraduate and graduate students with the competence and conscience necessary to serve criminal justice agencies and other organizations concerned with crime, justice, and community well-being.   The successful candidate will: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in both in-person and online formats; Maintain an active research agenda; Advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students; and Participate in departmental, university, professional, and community service.   Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Criminal Justice, Criminology, Justice Studies, or a closely related field. ABD candidates may be considered provided that all requirements for the doctorate will be completed by August 1, 2027. Evidence of effective college- or university-level teaching or demonstrated potential for teaching excellence. Evidence of an active research agenda and potential for continued scholarly productivity. Effective written and oral communication skills. A commitment to student advising and mentoring. A commitment to the missions of the Department of Criminal Justice and Xavier University, including Xavier’s Jesuit Catholic educational tradition.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching criminal justice courses at the undergraduate or graduate level. Ability to teach criminal justice research methods, policing courses, or both. Experience teaching in online formats.   The Department of Criminal Justice is part of the College of Health and Human Sciences . CHHS is a leader in experiential learning: 100% of our undergraduate and graduate programs require hands-on learning through field placements, internships, research experiences, and clinical opportunities. In the College of Health and Human Sciences, our commitment to exceptional teaching and mentoring drives us. We focus on scholarship and service in a variety of fields that make a direct and meaningful impact on others. We intentionally strive to create a learning experience that supports all students, incorporates a broad range of perspectives, and fosters an environment of belonging. In alignment with Xavier's Jesuit Catholic mission and Statement of Purpose to \"form students who change the world for the better,\" we are united across our diverse areas by the shared mission of changing human lives for the better .   Many of our College programs, including Department of Criminal Justice is part of Xavier Health, the University's integrated health initiative connecting a broad portfolio of programs and creating opportunities for collaboration across disciplines. Xavier Health offers more than 15 undergraduate and 12 graduate pathways, more than 500 community partnership sites, and connections across disciplines that contribute to health and human well-being. Xavier Health prepares servant-leaders through real-world experiences and Jesuit Catholic formation that puts the whole person at the center of care.  Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. Review of applications will start on October 26, 2026 with anticipated on-campus interviews anticipated toward the end of 2026.  Applications will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.   To receive full consideration, applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) up to three selected publications, combined into a single file; (4) evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as student or peer evaluations, if available, combined into a single file; and (5) the names and contact information of three professional references. The letter of interest should address the position’s qualifications and describe the applicant’s teaching philosophy, research agenda, and record of professional and institutional service or plans to contribute in these areas. Application materials should be submitted through Xavier University’s website. Letters of recommendation will be requested following initial screening interviews.   Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Cheryl Lero Jonson, Chair of the Department of Criminal Justice and Search Committee Chair, at jonsonc@xavier.edu or 513-745-1069.   Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor--Dept-of-Speech--Language-and-Communication-Science_JR100853": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Dept. of Speech, Language and Communication Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor, Dept. of Speech, Language and Communication Sciences ‌ The Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences (SLCS) at Xavier University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning Fall 2027. We seek a collaborative teacher-scholar who is excited to help build a new academic program from the ground up and whose teaching and clinical expertise will strengthen the Department's undergraduate curriculum in speech-language pathology.  The teaching expectation is 18 credit hours annually for this tenure-track faculty position when a faculty member meets the College’s active scholarship standards.  SLCS currently offers an undergraduate program in speech, language, and communication sciences, with a graduate program in speech-language pathology planned to launch in 2031. Consistent with Xavier University's mission, the Department seeks to equip students with the competence and conscience necessary to serve individuals with communication disorders and the professionals and communities who support them.  The successful candidate will:  Teach undergraduate courses in speech-language pathology, with the opportunity to help shape graduate-level curriculum as the Department's graduate program develops toward its planned 2031 launch;  Supervise students in clinical and practicum experiences as part of SLCS's experiential learning sequence;  Maintain an active research agenda;  Advise and mentor undergraduate (and, in time, graduate) students; and  Participate in departmental, university, professional, and community service.  Required Qualifications  A Ph.D. in Speech-Language Pathology, Communication Sciences and Disorders, or a closely related field. ABD candidates may be considered provided that all requirements for the doctorate will be completed by August 1, 2027.  A Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP) from the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association (ASHA), or eligibility to obtain CCC-SLP prior to appointment.  Experience supervising students in a clinical, practicum, or clinical fellowship (CFY) setting (any one of these is sufficient).  Evidence of effective college- or university-level teaching or demonstrated potential for teaching excellence.  Evidence of an active or emerging research agenda and potential for continued scholarly productivity.  Effective written and oral communication skills.  A commitment to student advising and mentoring.  A commitment to the missions of the Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences and Xavier University, including Xavier's Jesuit Catholic educational tradition.  Preferred Qualifications  We welcome applicants with clinical and research interests across all areas of speech-language pathology.  Experience or interest in contributing to the development of a new academic program.  Experience teaching undergraduate courses in speech-language pathology or communication sciences and disorders.  The Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences is part of the College of Health and Human Sciences . CHHS is a leader in experiential learning: 100% of our undergraduate and graduate programs require hands-on learning through field placements, internships, research experiences, and clinical opportunities. In the College of Health and Human Sciences, our commitment to exceptional teaching and mentoring drives us. We focus on scholarship and service in a variety of fields that make a direct and meaningful impact on others. We intentionally strive to create a learning experience that supports all students, incorporates a broad range of perspectives, and fosters an environment of belonging. In alignment with Xavier's Jesuit Catholic mission and Statement of Purpose to “form students who change the world for the better,” we are united across our diverse areas by the shared mission of changing human lives for the better .  Many of our College programs, including the Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences, are part of Xavier Health, the University's integrated health initiative connecting a broad portfolio of programs and creating opportunities for collaboration across disciplines. Xavier Health offers more than 15 undergraduate and 12 graduate pathways, more than 500 community partnership sites, and connections across disciplines that contribute to health and human well-being. Xavier Health prepares servant-leaders through real-world experiences and Jesuit Catholic formation that puts the whole person at the center of care.  Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests.   Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026, with anticipated interviews taking place in late October into November.  Applications will be accepted until the position closes at the University's discretion. To receive full consideration, applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) up to three selected publications, combined into a single file; (4) evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as student or peer evaluations, if available, combined into a single file; and (5) the names and contact information of three professional references. The letter of interest should address the position's qualifications and describe the applicant's teaching philosophy, research agenda, clinical and supervisory experience (as applicable), and record of professional and institutional service or plans to contribute in these areas. Application materials should be submitted through Xavier University's website.  Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Carrie Rountrey, Chair of the Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences and Search Committee Chair, at rountreyc@xavier.edu   or 513-745-4286. Administrative inquiries may be directed to Cathy Lee at leec29@xavier.edu or 513-745-3518.  Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity employer. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor-of-Instruction--Marketing_JR100855": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction, Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor of Instruction, Marketing ‌ The Williams College of Business at Xavier University invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Instruction position in the Department of Marketing beginning Fall 2027. The Williams College of Business is AACSB accredited. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts and is strongly committed to Ignatian Belonging. These values are central to our mission. We strive for a climate of respect and belonging that welcomes and supports members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We are committed unreservedly to open and free inquiry, and we deliberately seek out multiple perspectives.   The Assistant Professor of Instruction position is renewable on a yearly basis, with the potential after six years for promotion to Associate Professor of Instruction with a rolling two-year renewable contract. The candidate must be committed to providing quality teaching and to either (a) maintaining an active professional presence or (b) conducting scholarly research in compliance with AACSB standards for faculty. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.   Duties:   Faculty members at Xavier University are expected to teach for both in-person and online modalities in our undergraduate and master's programs (MBA). The successful candidate will be able to teach courses in General Marketing (e.g., Introduction to Marketing and Marketing Capstone) and upper-division electives. The ideal candidate will have demonstratable expertise in Sales, Marketing Research, MarTech, or Category Management. The Williams College of Business places a strong emphasis on experientially-based teaching and the successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to incorporate hands-on, professional engagement in the classroom. Other duties include service and participation in the life of the Department and University consistent with the mission of Jesuit higher education, and professional development activities on- and off-campus. Teaching load is four courses per semester.     Required Qualifications: Applicants for this non-tenure track faculty position must have at least a master's degree with a minimum of 18 graduate hours in marketing-related course work and a minimum of three years of professional work experience in the area of the teaching assignment . Strong candidates will have compelling evidence of teaching effectiveness, an active professional or scholarly agenda, and relevant professional work experience. The successful candidate will be able to engage diverse groups of students in learning opportunities.   We are strongly committed to enhancing Ignatian Belonging as it is central to our mission. Candidates who have worked with a diverse range of faculty, staff, and students and who can contribute to our mission of belonging are encouraged to identify their experiences and interests. Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity employer. To ensure consideration, applicants should submit their cover letter, curriculum vitae, evidence of teaching effectiveness, sample syllabi, and the names and contact information for three references on Xavier University's website. Applications will be reviewed immediately and accepted until the position closes at the University's discretion. Please direct requests for additional information to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Richie L. Liu,  liur2@xavier.edu . ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Dean--College-of-Nursing_JR100861": {
      "title": "Dean, College of Nursing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Dean, College of Nursing ‌ Xavier University, a Jesuit Catholic university in Cincinnati, Ohio, seeks an innovative, collaborative, and visionary individual committed to promoting and fostering excellence in teaching, research, professional practice, and service as the next Dean of the College of Nursing. The college is among the nation's leaders in holistic nursing and proud to be among the select nursing schools to receive the American Holistic Nurses Credentialing Corporation’s (AHNCC) endorsement. Reporting to the Provost, the Dean will bring the leadership and management qualities to build on the college's strengths and take it to even higher levels of academic excellence and student success. The Dean will collaborate with the faculty and staff to promote the college’s mission, advance strategic priorities, and create an environment that encourages growth and innovation. The Dean will foster scholarship and research along with partnerships with community partners. As a member of the Provost Area Leadership Team, the Dean will be expected to work collaboratively with the Deans across the University to ensure excellent programs that serve students, promote Xavier’s Jesuit Catholic values, and serve the community in Cincinnati and across the United States. The College of Nursing is an integral part of Xavier Health, Xavier’s flourishing ecosystem of health programs. As a leader within Xavier Health, the next Dean of Nursing will promote the breadth and distinctive strengths of Xavier’s health programs, build strong relationships across the institution-wide health portfolio, and foster interdisciplinary and interprofessional education, practice, research, and service. The ideal candidate will demonstrate an appreciation of and commitment to Xavier’s Jesuit Catholic mission with an ability to embed this mission into the life and priorities of the college. In addition, the next Dean will be student-focused; possess excellent interpersonal, communication, administrative, and organizational skills; and demonstrate the ability to articulate a vision that encourages and inspires quality program growth.   Key Responsibilities: Leadership In consultation with faculty, creates an environment and implements strategies to encourage exemplary teaching, scholarship, and service, integrating the Jesuit Catholic tradition. Inspires confidence, motivates others for engagement and innovation and addresses conflict constructively and fairly. Provides leadership and support for approximately 25 full-time faculty, 150 adjunct clinical faculty, and 11 staff members within the College of Nursing. Engages in strategic planning. Establishes an environment that values collaboration and inclusiveness. Promotes and facilitates the development of innovative and sustainable academic programs that respond to student, workforce, community, and healthcare needs while maintaining academic quality and appropriate faculty and clinical resources.   Financial Management In collaboration with the Vice Presidents, Deans, and XU Council, plans and evaluates the College’s budget and related activities to ensure alignment with the mission, strategic priorities, and policies of the University. Develops, administers, and monitors the College’s budget; advocates for adequate resources to support academic programs, faculty, staff, and student success; and maintains ultimate responsibility for the College’s fiscal management. Relationship Building Represents the college and the university at the city, state, and national levels. Partners with University Advancement to cultivate relationships with alumni, donors, foundations, healthcare organizations, and other external partners to advance philanthropic support for the college. Represents the college at the Provost Area Leadership Team and President’s Cabinet meetings. Seeks opportunities to collaborate with other Deans and stakeholders across the University. Seeks opportunities to establish collaborative relationships with the community. Builds strong relationships with faculty and staff and fosters a culture of collaboration, shared governance, professional development, and mutual respect.    Management Serves as an advocate for faculty and staff. Oversees the hiring process and evaluation of faculty and staff. Makes recommendations regarding reappointments, promotion, tenure, and sabbaticals. Monitors the implementation of the Strategic Plan and Systematic Evaluation Plan. Evaluates administrators and staff. Develops and upholds policies and procedures consistent with the student and faculty handbooks, College bylaws, and University policies Accreditation Submits pertinent accreditation and regulatory documents and reports to the Ohio Board of Nursing, the American Association of Colleges of Nursing (AACN), and the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE). Serves as the Ohio Board of Nursing Program Administrator for all pre-licensure programs. Oversees assessment and reporting activities to maintain specialized and institutional accreditation for the college's educational programs. Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate from an accredited institution with at least one graduate degree in nursing. Minimum of five years of experience in academic nursing, including demonstrated higher education administrative and leadership experience. Eligible for licensure as a registered professional nurse in Ohio. Record of achievement in teaching, scholarship, and service, that merits appointment as a tenured associate or full professor within the college. Demonstrated experience in academic administration, faculty leadership, program development, strategic planning, and/or organizational management. Demonstrated commitment to academic excellence, student success, collaboration, inclusion and innovation. Experience with accreditation, assessment, and regulatory requirements within nursing or higher education. For additional information regarding this position and the Xavier University College of Nursing, please see here . To ensure consideration, qualified/interested applicants must submit a cover letter, resume and names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University's website.  Applications will be reviewed immediately and will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion. Questions may be sent to the Search Committee Co-Chair, Dr. Catherine Frank at frankc4@xavier.edu . Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Exercise-Science_JR100848": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant/Associate Professor, Exercise Science ‌ The Exercise Science program, located in the School of Sport Science and Management in the College of Health and Human Sciences, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor position in Exercise Science beginning in Fall 2027. The School of Sport Science & Management offers undergraduate degrees in Exercise Science, Health Science and Wellness, Sport Management/Marketing, as well as master's degrees in Athletic Training, and Sport Administration.   The Exercise Science program’s teaching and research laboratory is housed in the Health United Building , a state-of-the-art facility that was designed as a national model of excellence for collegiate academic, health, wellness, and recreational services. Some equipment that is available for teaching and research in the exercise science laboratory include: COSMED K5 portable metabolic system, ActiGraph wGT3X-BT accelerometers, activPAL4 activity monitors (to measure sitting, standing, and stepping behavior), Fibion Research triaxial accelerometers, Meta Quest 3: Next-Gen Mixed Reality Headset, Polar heart rate monitors, Bod Pod, Functional Movement Screening (FMS) and BlazePod Trainer kits, Quark T12x Diagnostic grade 12-Lead Wireless ECG, SunTech Tango M2 Exercise and Stress Automatic Blood Pressure Monitor, Omron HEM-907XL Professional Blood Pressure Machine, MOXY Muscle Oxygen Monitor, MicroQuark spirometer, Nova Biomedical Lactate Plus blood lactate meters, Lange skin fold calipers, Cybex isokinetic dynamometer, hand grip dynamometers, Trackmaster TMX428 treadmills, and Velotron and Monark cycle ergometers.   Qualifications Earned doctorate in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Health Science, or related field. ABD applicants will be considered but must complete all requirements for their doctoral degree by August 2027. Preference will be given to candidates with NSCA and/or ACSM certification(s) and demonstrated potential to meet research expectations. To be considered for the associate professor position, candidates must have a minimum of five years teaching experience at an accredited college or university and a clearly-defined record of scholarship and publications.   Position Nine-month contract with the potential for summer teaching opportunities.   Salary/Rank Assistant/Associate Professor with salary commensurate to qualifications and experience.   Responsibilities include: Teaching undergraduate courses within the Exercise Science curriculum, including but not limited to Introduction to Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology and Lab, Nutrition for Sport & Exercise, Exercise Training Principles, Exercise Testing and Prescription, Biomechanics, Sports Psychology, Research Methods, Sport Science, Cardiopulmonary Testing and Prescription, Fitness in Special Populations. The teaching expectation is 18 credit hours annually for this tenure-track faculty position when a faculty member meets the College's active scholarship standards. Maintaining an active program of scholarship consistent with expectations for tenure and promotion. Advising and mentoring students regarding academic planning, professional development, and career opportunities. Participating in program, school, college, and university service activities.   The Exercise Science program is part of the College of Health and Human Sciences . CHHS is a leader in experiential learning: 100% of our undergraduate and graduate programs require hands-on learning through field placements, internships, research experiences, and clinical opportunities. In the College of Health and Human Sciences, our commitment to exceptional teaching and mentoring drives us. We focus on scholarship and service in a variety of fields that make a direct and meaningful impact on others. We intentionally strive to create a learning experience that supports all students, incorporates a broad range of perspectives, and fosters an environment of belonging. In alignment with Xavier's Jesuit Catholic mission and Statement of Purpose to \"form students who change the world for the better,\" we are united across our diverse areas by the shared mission of changing human lives for the better . Many of our College programs, including Exercise Science, are part of Xavier Health, the University's integrated health initiative connecting a broad portfolio of programs and creating opportunities for collaboration across disciplines. Xavier Health offers more than 15 undergraduate and 12 graduate pathways, more than 500 community partnership sites, and connections across disciplines that contribute to health and human well-being. Xavier Health prepares servant-leaders through real-world experiences and Jesuit Catholic formation that puts the whole person at the center of care. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests.   Xavier’s urban location in Cincinnati allows faculty to work with community partners to develop engaged learning and internship opportunities. Xavier is a member of the Association of Jesuit Colleges and Universities as well as the Big East.   Application To ensure consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information of three professional references on Xavier University's website by October 5, 2026 .   If you have any questions about this position, please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Jeremy Steeves at  steevesj@xavier.edu     ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor-of-Instruction--Biology_JR100846": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction, Biology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor of Instruction, Biology ‌ Xavier University invites applications for a renewable/permanent non-tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Biology to begin in Fall 202 7 . The individual must hold at least a M.S. degree in an area of the biological sciences, with experience relevant to human  physiology strongly preferred. This is not a remote position. Responsibilities include: teaching majors’ lectures and labs (e.g., Human Physiology) ,   non-science majors’ and allied health majors’ lectures and labs (e . g ., Human Biology, Anatomy and Physiology) , and s ervice to the department including preparation of one multi-section lab per term. Preparation of multi-section labs entails the planning and maintenance of course content, coordination with other faculty teaching the corequisite lecture a nd other sections of the lab, and working with the department lab manager to ensure that materials are ordered and set up correctly. Most of these are existing classes and already have materials prepared that will be shared.   Prior experience teaching college student labs, especially human physiology, is preferred. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.     The position is part of Xavier Health, the University's integrated health initiative connecting a broad portfolio of programs and creating opportunities for collaboration across disciplines.  Xavier Health offers more than 15 undergraduate and 12 graduate pathways, more than 500 community partnership sites, and connections across disciplines that contribute to health and human well-being.  Xavier Health prepares servant-leaders through real-world experiences and Jesuit Catholic formation that puts the whole person at the center of care.   Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We are firmly committed to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and strive to create a campus where everyone feels a strong sense of  belonging .   Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati . With its concentration of universities, research hospitals, and biotechnology companies, the region offers extensive opportunities for faculty to collaborate with community partners in developing research initiatives and immersive learning experiences.   Xavier is a member of the Association of Jesuit Colleges and Universities as well as the Big East Conference. The university continues to grow, with a strong focus on biomedical sciences and the proposed College of Osteopathic Medicine. Xavier is classified as a national university in the Carnegie Classifications and was recently recognized among the most innovative schools in the nation by U.S. News & World Report.   Applicants should submit the following to Xavier University’s website, an application letter, curriculum vitae and a statement of teaching philosophy that incorporates how you can support student belonging.  Review of applications will begin October 26, 2026 . Finalists will be asked for letters of recommendation. Questions may be sent to the Chair of the Department of Biology, Dr. Kathryn Morris , at morrisk10@xavier.edu.   ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Visiting-Faculty--Department-of-Biology_JR100849": {
      "title": "Visiting Faculty, Department of Biology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Visiting Faculty, Department of Biology ‌ Xavier University invites applications for a visiting faculty position in the Department of Biology to begin in Fall 202 7 , to complement its new undergraduate programs in Neuroscience. The successful candidate should bring a passion for teaching undergr aduates. This is not a remote position.   The pos ition is renewable annually for up to three years, pending continued need. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.   The individual must either b e a Ph.D. candidate or hold a Ph.D. in an area of the biological sciences . S pecialization in neuroscience requi red , with any area of neuroscience welcomed . Responsibilities include: teaching the equivalent of 4 courses per semester which may includ e courses in neuroscience, majors - level anatomy and/or physiology , professional skills courses for majors and/or other upper division courses of interest . Most of these are existing classes and already have materials prepared that will be shared.    Xavier is a member of the Association of Jesuit Colleges and Universities as well as the Big East. Xavier is growing, with life sciences a major focal direction. Xavier is a national university in the Carnegie classifications, and was recently named in the most innovative schools nationally by U.S. News and World Report.    At Xavier and in this department, we believe our people make all the difference in cultivating an inclusive environment that welcomes ideas, encourages innovation, and manifests belonging. We welcome candidates from all walks of life with different strengths, experiences, beliefs, and backgrounds to apply.    Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts and is strongly committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity. These values are central to our mission .  We strive for a climate of respect and inclusiveness that welcomes and supports members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences, is committed unreservedly to open and free inquiry, and deliberately seeks out multiple perspectives.   Applicants should submit the following to Xavier University’s website, an application letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy that incorporates how you can support student belonging .   Review of applications will begin January 4, 2027 . Finalists will be asked for letters of recommendation. Questions may be sent to the Chair of the Department of Biology, Dr. Kat Morris , at morrisk10@xavier.edu .   ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Groundskeeper-I_JR100840": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Groundskeeper I ‌ Xavier University is looking to hire a Groundskeeper for the Office of Physical Plant. The primary purpose of this position is to maintain a safe and beautiful campus according to Xavier standards. Includes but not limited to sports fields, landscaping, and mow crew assistance. JOB RESPONSIBILTIES: 1. Operates hand and power tools to cut, trim, edge grass, turf, and (maintain athletic fields by dragging, laying out, lining, and painting) applies chemicals, prunes trees and shrubs, trim hedges, mulches, removes snow, etc. All while wearing appropriate personal protective equipment and following all established safety procedures. 2. Applies top soil, grades surfaces; prepares seed beds, plants bulbs; trims hedges, shrubs, and trees; weeds flower beds, and removes trees and shrubs by lifting or moving heavy equipment or material un assisted up to 125 pounds. Lifts or moves heavier items by communicating with assistance. 3. Picks up litter, trash, and removes trash and recycling from cans; keeps records of work performed, time and material used and similar maintenance data and reports the same.  Also responsible for taking scrap metal recyclables to the recycling center. 4. Services and repairs, cleans, and performs daily and preventative maintenance on grounds equipment and shop. 5. Assists other departments in related activities (sets up and delivers equipment, furniture, supplies, and Christmas lights, etc.) JOB REQUIREMENTS: High school diploma or GED required Vocational or technical training preferred 1-3 years of relevant experience Valid driver’s license Pesticide license preferred Continuing education To ensure full consideration, interested and qualified applicants must submit a cover letter and resume on Xavier University’s website.  Review of applications will start on October 5, 2026 and will be accepted until the position closes at the University's discretion. Candidates selected for the final stages of the interview process will be asked to provide the names and contact information of three professional references. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Adjunct-Faculty---Department-of-Speech--Language--and-Communication-Sciences_JR100850": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-17\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Adjunct Faculty - Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences ‌ The Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences (SLCS) at Xavier University invites applications for Adjunct Instructors beginning immediately. We seek a collaborative educator who is excited to contribute to a new academic program and whose teaching and clinical expertise will strengthen the Department's undergraduate curriculum in speech-language pathology. SLCS currently offers an undergraduate program in speech, language, and communication sciences, with a graduate program in speech-language pathology planned to launch in 2031. Consistent with Xavier University's mission, the Department seeks to equip students with the competence and conscience necessary to serve individuals with communication disorders and the professionals and communities who support them. The Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences is part of the College of Health and Human Sciences . CHHS is a leader in experiential learning: 100% of our undergraduate and graduate programs require hands-on learning through field placements, internships, research experiences, and clinical opportunities. In the College of Health and Human Sciences, our commitment to exceptional teaching and mentoring drives us. We focus on scholarship and service in a variety of fields that make a direct and meaningful impact on others. We intentionally strive to create a learning experience that supports all students, incorporates a broad range of perspectives, and fosters an environment of belonging. In alignment with Xavier's Jesuit Catholic mission and Statement of Purpose to “form students who change the world for the better,” we are united across our diverse areas by the shared mission of changing human lives for the better . Many of our College programs, including the Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences, are part of Xavier Health, the University's integrated health initiative connecting a broad portfolio of programs and creating opportunities for collaboration across disciplines. Xavier Health offers more than 15 undergraduate and 12 graduate pathways, more than 500 community partnership sites, and connections across disciplines that contribute to health and human well-being. Xavier Health prepares servant-leaders through real-world experiences and Jesuit Catholic formation that puts the whole person at the center of care. The successful candidate will: Teach undergraduate courses in speech-language pathology, and later, graduate-level curriculum as the Department's graduate program develops toward its planned 2031 launch; Supervise students in clinical and practicum experiences as part of SLCS's experiential learning sequence; Advise and mentor undergraduate (and, in time, graduate) students. Required Qualifications A masters, clinical doctorate, or Ph.D. in Speech-Language Pathology, Communication Sciences and Disorders, or a closely related field. A Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP) from the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association (ASHA). Effective written and oral communication skills. A commitment to student advising and mentoring. A commitment to the missions of the Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences and Xavier University, including Xavier's Jesuit Catholic educational tradition. Preferred Qualifications Experience supervising students in a clinical, practicum, or clinical fellowship (CFY) setting (any one of these is sufficient). Evidence of effective college- or university-level teaching or demonstrated potential for teaching excellence. We welcome applicants with clinical and research interests across all areas of speech-language pathology. Experience teaching undergraduate courses in speech-language pathology or communication sciences and disorders. Review of applications is ongoing, based on timing and semester-to-semester needs. To receive full consideration, applicants should submit: (1) a letter of interest; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as student or peer evaluations, if available, combined into a single file; and (4) the names and contact information of three professional references. The letter of interest should address the position's qualifications and describe the applicant's teaching philosophy and clinical and supervisory experience (as applicable). Application materials should be submitted through December 1, 2026 . Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Carrie Rountrey, Chair of the Department of Speech, Language, and Communication Sciences and Search Committee Chair, at rountreyc@xavier.edu or 513-745-4286. Administrative inquiries may be directed to Cathy Lee at leec29@xavier.edu or 513-745-3518. We are happy to advise you on courses for which we are currently seeking instructors. ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor-of-Instruction--Accountancy_JR100865": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction, Accountancy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor of Instruction, Accountancy ‌ The Williams College of Business at Xavier University invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Instruction position in the Department of Accountancy and Business Law beginning fall 2027. The Williams College of Business is AACSB accredited. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts and is strongly committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity. These values are central to  our mission . We strive for a climate of respect and inclusiveness that welcomes and supports members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences, is committed unreservedly to open and free inquiry, and deliberately seeks out multiple perspectives. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.   Xavier’s urban location in Cincinnati allows faculty to work with community partners to develop engaged learning and internship opportunities. Xavier is a member of the Association of Jesuit Colleges and Universities as well as the Big East.    The Assistant Professor of Instruction position is renewable on a yearly basis, with the potential after six years for promotion to Associate Professor of Instruction with a rolling two-year renewable contract. The candidate must be committed to providing quality teaching and to maintaining an active and sustained connection to their field through professional engagement, scholarly activity, or a combination of the two. The successful candidate will demonstrate a clear plan for continued professional and/or scholarly engagement that supports currency in their discipline, informs their teaching, and contributes to their ongoing faculty qualifications.   Duties: Faculty members at Xavier are expected to teach in both undergraduate and master’s programs (MBA and/or MS in Accountancy) in live and on-line formats. The successful candidate will be able to teach both introductory courses, financial and managerial accounting, as well as an additional course in the major (e.g., Tax, Accounting Information Systems, Intermediate / Advanced Financial, Audit, etc.). In addition to teaching, the successful candidate will also be willing to serve as a faculty advisor for Accounting Society, which provides students with opportunities for professional development and leadership. Other duties include service and participation in the life of the Department and University consistent with the mission of Jesuit higher education, and professional development activities on and off campus. Teaching load is four courses per semester.   Required Qualifications: Applicants for this non-tenure track faculty position must have at least a master’s degree with a minimum of 18 graduate hours in accounting-related course work. Strong candidates will have compelling evidence of teaching effectiveness, relevant professional work experience, and an established or developing record of professional engagement and/or scholarly activity. Current professional certification (CPA or similar) is strongly preferred. All areas of teaching interest will be considered. The successful candidate will be able to engage diverse groups of students in learning opportunities.   Applications: To ensure consideration, applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, relevant teaching materials, a one-page statement outlining their long-term plan for maintaining a connection to business practice and/or scholarly engagement, and the names and contact information for three references on Xavier University’s website.   Review of applications will begin on October 30, 2026 and applications will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.   Professional and Scholarly Engagement Statement: Applicants should submit a one-page statement outlining their long-term plan for maintaining an active and sustained connection to their field and for maintaining their faculty qualifications. The statement should emphasize how the candidate will remain current in business practice and the professional community relevant to their area of teaching, including the types of professional engagement, industry interaction, continuing development, and other activities they anticipate pursuing to inform and enhance their teaching and maintain their qualifications as an Instructional Practitioner. Candidates whose qualification strategy includes scholarly academic engagement (i.e., publishing) may also describe their plans for developing and disseminating intellectual contributions. Overall, the statement should present a realistic and sustained plan for continued professional and/or scholarly engagement appropriate to the candidate's discipline, expertise, and career trajectory.   Please direct requests for additional information to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Megan Jones, Jonesm66@xavier.edu .   ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor--MSW-Program_JR100866": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, MSW Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor, MSW Program ‌ The College of Health and Human Services at Xavier University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position in the Department of Social Work beginning Fall 2027.  This tenure-track teaching position will be primarily assigned to the MSW Program currently in pre-candidacy.  Xavier University seeks experienced, innovative, and highly motivated candidates for a full-time, open-rank, tenure track faculty.   Responsibilities include teaching at the BSW and MSW levels, curriculum and program development, pursuing grant opportunities, academic student advising, participating in department/college/university/community service, and developing a scholarly agenda. The successful candidate should demonstrate a strong commitment to student-centered pedagogy, social justice, and engaged learning and have distance teaching and course development experience.   QUALIFICATIONS: Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree. While a doctoral degree in social work is preferred, related doctoral degrees will also be considered; A master’s social work degree from a CSWE-accredited program (or a CASWE-accredited degree recognized through an MOU with CSWE, or an ISWDRES-evaluated degree); Excellent communication skills and a strong commitment to working as part of a collaborative team; Passion for exciting and motivating students from diverse backgrounds; Contribution to a campus climate that supports equity, diversity, and inclusion.   Desirable Qualifications: At least two (2) years of post-master’s social work degree practice experience in social work; Previous full-time experience with instruction in social work education; Ability to teach across the curriculum, particularly policy and research courses; Experience with CSWE accreditation standards and processes. Demonstrated experience with program and curriculum development and management. Experience with online teaching and/or distance education program. Record of excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service.   Position: Nine-month faculty contract with summer teaching opportunities.   Salary/Rank: Assistant/Associate professor with salary commensurate to qualifications and experience.   Teaching Load: The teaching expectation is 18 credit hours annually for this tenure-track faculty position when a faculty member meets the College's active scholarship standards   The Department of Social Work is part of the College of Health and Human Sciences . CHHS is a leader in experiential learning: 100% of our undergraduate and graduate programs require hands-on learning  through field placements, internships, research experiences, and clinical opportunities. In the College of Health and Human Sciences, our commitment to exceptional teaching and mentoring drives us. We focus on scholarship and service in a variety of fields that make a direct and meaningful impact on others. We intentionally strive to create a learning experience that supports all students, incorporates a broad range of perspectives, and fosters an environment of belonging. In alignment with Xavier's Jesuit Catholic mission and Statement of Purpose to \"form students who change the world for the better,\" we are united across our diverse areas by the shared mission of changing human lives for the better . Many of our College programs, including Social Work, are part of Xavier Health, the University's integrated health initiative connecting a broad portfolio of programs and creating opportunities for collaboration across disciplines. Xavier Health offers more than 15 undergraduate and 12 graduate pathways, more than 500 community partnership sites, and connections across disciplines that contribute to health and human well-being. Xavier Health prepares servant-leaders through real-world experiences and Jesuit Catholic formation that puts the whole person at the center of care.  Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts. Guided by our  mission and values , we welcome and support members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences. We unreservedly commit to open and free inquiry, deliberately seek out multiple perspectives, and create a campus where everyone feels a sense of  belonging . Our campus is located in the vibrant and thriving city of  Cincinnati , which has an array of neighborhoods and activities to suit many interests. Application: For preferred consideration for this position, applications should be received no later than November 13, 2026 .  Submit letter of application, CV, and name, address and phone number of three references on Xavier University’s website.  Letters of application should describe the applicant’s qualifications, teaching philosophy, and research agenda. Questions may be directed to Jaylene Schaefer, the search committee chair, at  schaeferj1@xavier.edu . Applications will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.   Xavier University is an Equal Opportunity Employer   ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
    },
    "https://xavier.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/XavierCareers/job/Cincinnati-OH/Assistant-Professor-of-Instruction--Business-Law_JR100863": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction, Business Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nCurrent Xavier University employees must apply to the internal career site by logging into Workday Assistant Professor of Instruction, Business Law ‌ The Williams College of Business at Xavier University invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Instruction position in the Department of Accountancy and Business Law beginning fall 2027. The Williams College of Business is AACSB accredited. Xavier University is part of the 500-year-old Jesuit Catholic tradition of academic excellence in the liberal arts and is strongly committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity. These values are central to  our mission . We strive for a climate of respect and inclusiveness that welcomes and supports members from diverse backgrounds and life experiences, is committed unreservedly to open and free inquiry, and deliberately seeks out multiple perspectives. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.   Xavier’s urban location in Cincinnati allows faculty to work with community partners to develop engaged learning and internship opportunities. Xavier is a member of the Association of Jesuit Colleges and Universities as well as the Big East.    The Assistant Professor of Instruction position is renewable on a yearly basis, with the potential after six years for promotion to Associate Professor of Instruction with a rolling two-year renewable contract. The candidate must be committed to providing quality teaching and to maintaining an active and sustained connection to their field through professional engagement, scholarly activity, or a combination of the two. The successful candidate will demonstrate a clear plan for continued professional and/or scholarly engagement that supports currency in their discipline, informs their teaching, and contributes to their ongoing faculty qualifications.   Duties: Faculty members at Xavier are expected to teach in both undergraduate and master’s programs in live and on-line formats. Other duties include service and participation in the life of the Department and University consistent with the mission of Jesuit higher education, and professional development activities on and off campus. Teaching load is four courses per semester.   Required Qualifications: Applicants for this non-tenure track faculty position must have a terminal degree (JD or PhD) from an accredited law school. Strong candidates will have compelling evidence of teaching effectiveness, relevant professional work experience, and an established or developing record of professional engagement and/or scholarly activity. The successful candidate will be able to engage diverse groups of students in learning opportunities.   Applications: To ensure consideration, applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, relevant teaching materials, a one-page statement outlining their long-term plan for maintaining a connection to business practice and/or scholarly engagement, and the names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin on October 30, 2026 and applications will be accepted until the position closes at the University’s discretion.   Professional and Scholarly Engagement Statement: Applicants should submit a one-page statement outlining their long-term plan for maintaining an active and sustained connection to their field and for maintaining their faculty qualifications. The statement should emphasize how the candidate will remain current in business practice and the professional community relevant to their area of teaching, including the types of professional engagement, industry interaction, continuing development, and other activities they anticipate pursuing to inform and enhance their teaching and maintain their qualifications as an Instructional Practitioner. Candidates whose qualification strategy includes scholarly academic engagement (i.e., publishing) may also describe their plans for developing and disseminating intellectual contributions. Overall, the statement should present a realistic and sustained plan for continued professional and/or scholarly engagement appropriate to the candidate's discipline, expertise, and career trajectory.   Please direct requests for additional information to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Timothy Miller, millert17@xavier.edu .   ‌ Benefits - applies only to full-time positions:  Xavier University offers a wide array of complementary and affordable benefit options to meet the financial, educational, health, and wellness needs of you and your family.  Eligibility varies by position and employment class:  Comprehensive insurance plans including medical, dental, vision and prescription coverage. Tax advantaged accounts including health savings accounts, flexible spending accounts, and dependent care account. Financial security via life and long-term disability insurance, accident and illness insurance, and retirement savings plans. Generous paid time off work options including vacation, sick leave and holidays. Tuition remission for employees and their eligible dependents."
